# shell: desktop
# home: fixture
# splash: on
# The splash covers the desktop at its CURRENT size, not the size the
# window began at.  The desktop is widened while the boot screen is
# still up, and a corner beyond the first window's edge is asked for the
# black -- and, once the veil lifts, for the backdrop, which a pixel off
# the surface can never show, so the corner is proven to exist as well as
# to be covered.  Before the fix that corner showed the backdrop under
# the veil: it was painted over the 1000 by 680 the window started in,
# and a maximized desktop closed under a splash the size of its first
# window.
resize 1400 900
wait 1
expect-pixel 5 5 000000
expect-pixel 1390 890 000000
expect-pixel 1005 685 000000
note the far corner and the first pixel past the old edge are both
note under the veil, so the screen is covered rather than its first size
wait 150
expect-pixel 5 5 336698
expect-pixel 1390 890 336698
expect-pixel 1005 685 336698
note and the black is lifted off the whole of it: the backdrop is there
note at the corner that was under the veil, so the corner is real
quit
